{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem of seating 8 people around a square table with 2 people on each side, where rotations of the same seating arrangement are considered equivalent, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of arrangements without considering rotations:**\n   - First, we choose 2 people out of 8 to sit on the first side. This can be done in \\( \\binom{8}{2} \\) ways.\n   - Then, we choose 2 people out of the remaining 6 to sit on the second side. This can be done in \\( \\binom{6}{2} \\) ways.\n   - Next, we choose 2 people out of the remaining 4 to sit on the third side. This can be done in \\( \\binom{4}{2} \\) ways.\n   - Finally, the last 2 people will sit on the fourth side. This can be done in \\( \\binom{2}{2} \\) ways.\n   - After choosing the people for each side, we need to arrange them in the 2 seats on each side. This can be done in \\(2! \\) (2 factorial) ways for each side.\n   - Therefore, the total number of arrangements without considering rotations is:\n     \\[\n     \\binom{8}{2} \\times \\binom{6}{2} \\times \\binom{4}{2} \\times \\binom{2}{2} \\times (2!)^4 = 28 \\times 15 \\times 6 \\times 1 \\times 16 = 40320\n     \\]\n\n","prefix_end":1145,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,315,37299,220,23,1251,2163,264,9334,1965,448,220,17,1251,389,1817,3108,11,1380,69201,315,279,1852,37299,26112,525,6509,13578,11,582,646,1795,1493,7354,1447,16,13,3070,47866,279,2790,1372,315,27804,2041,12831,69201,25,1019,256,481,5512,11,582,5157,220,17,1251,700,315,220,23,311,2444,389,279,1156,3108,13,1096,646,387,2814,304,17767,1124,6863,316,90,23,15170,17,92,1124,8,5510,624,256,481,5005,11,582,5157,220,17,1251,700,315,279,9664,220,21,311,2444,389,279,2086,3108,13,1096,646,387,2814,304,17767,1124,6863,316,90,21,15170,17,92,1124,8,5510,624,256,481,9295,11,582,5157,220,17,125